om filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 36.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $156.1m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 7 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"},{"text":"Gross margin of 50.8% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $73.2m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-0.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 52.1% to 50.8% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2000178/000119312526210585/0001193125-26-210585-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-210585"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 43.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.43,"consecutive":2,"current":0.508,"current_display":"50.8%","threshold_display":"43.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 18.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.18,"consecutive":2,"current":0.361,"current_display":"36.1%","threshold_display":"18.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.001,"current_display":"-0.1%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.30","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.3,"consecutive":1,"current":0.805,"current_display":"0.81","threshold_display":"1.30","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive th